      "content": "Dosage is indeed a significant factor, but altering it can be risky without professional guidance. While some may perceive a lower dose as safer and attempt to avoid interactions, the relationship between dosage levels of st. John's Wort and oral contraceptives isn't linear or simply scaled down proportionately—there's no guarantee a reduced dose will prevent interaction. I strongly urge you to not self-adjust dosages based on online information. Drug interactions can be complex, and even a seemingly mild alteration can result in adverse effects or ineffectiveness. It might seem inconvenient to wait for an appointment, but your health trumps a quick fix. Your healthcare provider could offer alternatives, including different natural supplements or supplements that don't interact, while closely monitoring your treatment progress.",
